You convert ONE file of a Node.js (CommonJS) Express backend from Sequelize/Postgres to Mongoose/MongoDB.
Hard rules:
1. Reply with ONLY the complete new file inside one ```javascript block. No explanations. No new npm packages.
2. Keep every exported name, every function signature, the same HTTP status codes, the same error classes
   (require("../helper/customErrors")) thrown in the SAME ORDER, and EXACTLY the same response JSON shapes.
   Preserve the original's observable behaviour, INCLUDING its bugs (if the original crashes with a 500 in some
   case, the new code must also throw there, after the same side effects).
3. Data access ONLY through `const { User, Article, Comment, Tag, Favorite, Follower, mongoose, nextId } = require("../models")`
   (path relative to the file). Models listed below. Prefer `.lean()` reads and build plain response objects
   explicitly; there is no `dataValues`, no `toJSON` magic, no Sequelize association methods.
4. Never send `_id`, `password`, `authorId`, `articleId` or internal fields to clients unless the response
   shape lists them. Users have integer `_id` (the old `id`). Comments expose `id` (= their integer `_id`).
5. New users/articles/comments get `_id: await nextId("users"|"articles"|"comments")`. Tags use the tag name as `_id`.
6. Compound `_id` documents (Favorite, Follower): always match with dotted paths, e.g.
   `{ "_id.userId": a, "_id.followerId": b }`; insert with `updateOne({ "_id.userId": a, "_id.followerId": b },
   { $setOnInsert: { _id: { userId: a, followerId: b } } }, { upsert: true })`, keys in exactly the listed order.
7. Counters (`followersCount`, `favoritesCount`): change them ONLY when a junction document was really inserted
   (`res.upsertedCount === 1`) or deleted (`res.deletedCount === 1`), inside the same transaction:
   `const s = await mongoose.startSession(); await s.withTransaction(async () => { ...ops with { session: s }... }); await s.endSession();`
8. Sequelize timestamps map to Mongoose `timestamps: true` (createdAt/updatedAt are set automatically).

MODELS (generated from the reviewed schema; you cannot change them):
- Article (collection articles): _id:Number(=Articles.id), slug:string, title:string, description:string, body:string, createdAt:date, updatedAt:date, authorId:int, tagList:[String] (embedded TagList), favoritesCount:Number (counter of Favorites.articleId, YOU must $inc/$dec it). Indexes: {"slug": 1}; {"createdAt": -1}; {"authorId": 1, "createdAt": -1}; {"tagList": 1, "createdAt": -1}
- Comment (collection comments): _id:Number(=Comments.id), body:string, createdAt:date, updatedAt:date, articleId:int, authorId:int. Indexes: {"articleId": 1}
- Tag (collection tags): _id:String(=tag name). Indexes: -
- User (collection users): _id:Number(=Users.id), email:string, username:string, bio:string, image:string, password:string, createdAt:date, updatedAt:date, followersCount:Number (counter of Followers.userId, YOU must $inc/$dec it). Indexes: {"username": 1}; {"email": 1}
- Favorite (collection favorites): _id:{articleId,userId} compound. Indexes: {"_id.articleId": 1}; {"_id.userId": 1}
- Follower (collection followers): _id:{userId,followerId} compound. Indexes: {"_id.followerId": 1}; {"_id.userId": 1}

RESPONSE SHAPES the endpoints of this file must produce (from the original app):
- GET /api/user -> 200: {user:{bio:str|null,email:str,image:str|null,token:str,username:str}}
- PUT /api/user -> 200: {user:{bio:str,image:str,token:str,username:str}}
--- already converted middleware/authentication.js (use its exports as-is) ---
const { NotFoundError } = require("../helper/customErrors");
const { jwtVerify } = require("../helper/jwt");
const { User } = require("../models");

const verifyToken = async (req, res, next) => {
  try {
    const { headers } = req;
    if (!headers.authorization) return next();

    const token = headers.authorization.split(" ")[1];
    if (!token) throw new SyntaxError("Token missing or malformed");

    const userVerified = await jwtVerify(token);
    if (!userVerified) throw new Error("Invalid Token");

    const user = await User.findOne({ email: userVerified.email })
      .select("-email")
      .lean();

    if (!user) {
      return next(new NotFoundError("User"));
    }

    req.loggedUser = user;
    headers.email = userVerified.email;
    req.loggedUser.token = token;

    next();
  } catch (error) {
    next(error);
  }
};

module.exports = verifyToken;


